member.summary:
Adjust the width of the ScrollViewer when its content is resized.
If the vertical scroll bar is not visible, the with of the ScrollViewer should equal its content;
Otherwise, the scroll bar width should be accounted for.

This override is called whenever the view lines containing our adornments are edited or go out of view.
We use this override to keep our bind variable manager in sync with changes to the bind variable tokens;
specifically, to handle deletes and renames.

Returns the proper color for the indicator based on the input parameters.

Values array must be:
{(Boolean) SubtypeFieldHasCommitError, (DesignViewEditState) SubtypeFieldEditState, (Boolean) DefaultSubtypeHasCommitError, (DesignViewEditState) DefaultSubtypeEditState}

Returns the proper width for the indicator based on the input parameters.

Values array must be:
{(Boolean) SubtypeFieldHasCommitError, (DesignViewEditState) SubtypeFieldEditState, (Boolean) DefaultSubtypeHasCommitError, (DesignViewEditState) DefaultSubtypeEditState}

Determines the correct fill/background color for our view indicators and returns the corresponding brush.

Values array must be:
{(DesignViewEditState) EditState, (Boolean) HasValidationError, (Boolean) HasCommitWarning, (Boolean) HasCommitError}

Determines the correct width for our view indicators and returns the corresponding value.

Values array must be:
{(DesignViewEditState) EditState, (Boolean) HasValidationError, (Boolean) HasCommitWarning, (Boolean) HasCommitError}
OR
{(Boolean)HasValidationError, (Boolean)HasValidationWarning}

if the given member is already present in the set. then replaces all existing oids for the member with the given IEnumerable, but,
if the given member is not already present in the set. then adds oids for the member using the given IEnumerable.
So in other words, this is a "generous Replace" rather than a "strict" one.

member.remarks:
Example: When using an ItemTemplate with a ListBox, use the following in an
event handler for a contained control to get the ListBoxItem.
ListBoxItem lbi = Util.GetParentOfType<ListBoxItem>(sender as DependencyObject);

